SUMMARY:Speed / Power
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3600 kcal\, 170 g protein\, 550 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: 80-110 g carbs in the 2-3 hours before running\, 
 25-35 g protein after\, and another carb-heavy meal within 2 hours.\nCate
 gory: sprint\nRun volume: 3 km\n\n\nAdjustments:\n- Protective changes fr
 om prior-month body-part feedback.\n- Reduced for prior-month recovery fe
 edback.\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 10 min easy plus skips\, ankling\, and 3 relaxed
  strides.\n\n\nMain Work:\n- Plyometrics: pogos 3 x 20 sec and low broad 
 jumps 3 x 3 at crisp RPE 6-7.\n- Hill sprint technique: 4-6 x 8-12 sec at
  sprint RPE 7-8 with full walk-back recovery.\n- Stop if mechanics soften
  or symptoms are worse the next morning.\n- Lower-body feedback: use the 
 safest comfortable range and stop if joints or back flare.\n\n\nRun:\n- P
 lanned running volume: 3 km.\n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep pro
 tein near target\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\n
 \nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints fe
 el stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
