 5 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protein
  in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again aft
 er.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 5-10 min easy movem
 ent\, joint prep\, and 2-3 gradual ramp sets before loading.\n\n\nOptiona
 l Activation (before lifting):\n- Weighted hyperextensions: 2 x 12 at 10 
 kg\; RPE 5-6.\n\n\nCompound Lifts — rest 3–4 min between sets:\n1. Ha
 ck squat: 4 x 6 at 80 kg added weight\; RPE 7-8.\n2. Romanian deadlift: 4
  x 6 at 85 kg\; RPE 7-8.\n\n\nAccessories — rest 90–150 sec between s
 ets:\n3. Seated hamstring curl: 3 x 10 at 40 kg\; RPE 8.\n4. Calf raises:
  3 x 12 at 60 kg\; RPE 8.\n5. Tibialis raises: 2 x 15 at 15 kg\; RPE 7-8.
 \n\n\nCore:\n6. Pallof press: 2 x 12 per side at 10 kg\; RPE 7.\n7. Front
  plank: 2 x 45-60 seconds at 45\; Leave form in reserve.\n\n\nSession Not
 es:\n- The expected duration is 90-120 minutes.\n- Compound work stops wi
 th about two repetitions in reserve.\n- Accessories stop with one to thre
 e repetitions in reserve.\n- No routine set is taken to failure.\n- If a 
 prescribed starting load exceeds RPE 8 on the first working set\, reduce 
 it immediately by 5-10%\; do not force the written number.\n\n\nFueling:\
 n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates 
 before and after training.\n\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:
 00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.\n\n\nProgression & Guardrails:\n-
  Complete every set with clean form and about 2 reps left. Then use the n
 ext scheduled weight\, or the smallest increase after reaching the top of
  the rep/time range\; otherwise repeat. Keep activation and reduced sessi
 ons at the listed dose.
