DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Zone-5 Intervals
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 165 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 80-110 g carbs in the 2-3 hours before running\, 2
 5-35 g protein after\, and another carb-heavy meal within 2 hours.\nCateg
 ory: quality_run\nRun volume: 9 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 5-10 min easy movemen
 t\, joint prep\, and 2-3 gradual ramp sets before loading.\n\n\nMain Work
 :\n- 2 km at 5:30-6:00/km\, then 3 relaxed strides.\n- 3:50-4:00/km\; RPE
  8-9\, start at the slower end\n- 5 x 3 minutes\n- 2 minutes of easy jogg
 ing at 5:45-6:20/km between repetitions.\n- 1.5-2 km at 5:35-6:10/km\, ad
 justed to the prescribed total.\n- Ab-wheel rollout from knees: 2 x 6-8\;
  bodyweight\, short controlled range\, RPE 6. Substitute front plank 2 x 
 30 seconds if control is lost.\n- Banded flutter kicks: 2 x 15-20 seconds
  alternating legs\; light resistance\, ribs down and pelvis still\, RPE 5
 -6.\n- Aim for zone 5 late in the repetitions if heart-rate zones are est
 ablished\; do not sprint to chase the number.\n- Effort takes priority ov
 er pace. If the easy warm-up still feels unusually hard or the legs remai
 n heavy\, replace quality work with 30-40 minutes easy at RPE 2-4\; do no
 t make up the hard work.\n- Do core after the run and cool-down\, resting
  45-60 seconds between sets. Shorten the range or stop for back or hip di
 scomfort\; halve or omit core when fatigued.\n\n\nRun:\n- Planned running
  volume: 9 km.\n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near targ
 et\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\n\nRecovery:\n-
  Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
